NEARS-3555 AC3 live repro — DeliveryApp (Android emulator-5554, via scripts/qa-run.sh)
Setup: DeliveryApp/android/app/google-services.json removed (mv'd to .bak); same
conditional-plugin-application mechanism as the other two apps
(build.gradle.kts:10-13).

`scripts/qa-run.sh --root <worktree> DeliveryApp emulator-5554` console output:
I/flutter ( 5555): [FAIL] endpoint=null http_status=null type=FirebaseInitFailure msg="firebase init failed (PlatformException)"

Count check: grep -c "type=FirebaseInitFailure" -> 1 (exactly one line)

App continued past the failure normally (NET/config-fetch attempts followed,
no crash, no red screen, firebaseReady=false, fail-safe intact):
I/flutter ( 5555): [NET] GET endpoint=/api/v1/config
I/flutter ( 5555): [FAIL] endpoint=/api/v1/config http_status=null type=ApiFailure msg="api request threw" correlation_id=3847531e-8023-45c1-8479-80b05cae4909
(the ApiFailure line is the SEPARATE, pre-existing splash config-fetch failure —
expected since no backend is running for this client-only ticket; unrelated to
the Firebase-init catch arms under test.)

Baseline (config present) run immediately before this one: 0 hits for
"FirebaseInitFailure" — confirms no over-logging on the success path.

Regression item 3 (duplicate-app path never logs) and items 4-5 (PII-safe
reason string; no over-logging on the duplicate-app early-return-true branch)
were verified by DIRECT STATIC READ of the landed diff (55e23e852), not a live
repro: triggering a genuine `duplicate-app` FirebaseException requires calling
Firebase.initializeApp() a second time in-process, which is not naturally
reachable from a normal boot without instrumenting/modifying app code — QA does
not edit product code. Confirmed structurally in all 3 apps' main.dart:
`if (e.code == 'duplicate-app') { return true; }` returns BEFORE any
AppLogger.failure(...) call in every arm, and the one AppLogger.failure(...)
call site per arm passes `'firebase init failed (${e.runtimeType})'` — never
`e.message`/`e.toString()`/the raw caught object — matching the PII allow-list.

google-services.json restored immediately after this test (mv back from .bak).
